# {{title}}

{{description}}

Modern WordPress plugin featuring an MVC style structure, dependency injection container, Composer autoloading, Docker support, and Webpack build pipeline.

## Structure

All php files reside in `inc`. All `psr-4` classes will be autoloaded via `composer` from the `inc/app` folder. Controllers and Services are registered to the Container in the main php file. Controllers are responsible for registering hooks to wordpress.

All raw js, css, and blocks reside in `src`. These are files that need to be built during the build process.

## Usage

### Docker

Docker set up to control the development environment. You must have `docker` and `docker-compose` installed.

Docker env variables for php and wordpress versions will be set in `.env`. The wordpress `debug.log` file from the docker container will be placed in the projects root directory.

### Dev Scripts

To build.
    
```bash
npm run build

```

To develop.

```bash
docker compose up -d

npm run dev

```

To archive for distribution run.

```bash
npm run archive:dist

```

To archive the entire development package.

```bash
npm run archive:dev

```

## Blocks

### Create a block

Use the `create:block` npm script supplied.

```bash
npm run create:block

```

The script will create your block files. Its recommended to install the files in `src/blocks`. Block files will use typescript by default. Edit the `block.json` file to your liking. The `create:block` script uses basically the same templates wordpress does `https://github.com/WordPress/gutenberg/tree/trunk/packages/create-block/lib/templates/block`. They have been modified slightly for use with typescript.

### Register a block

Once you have successfully created a block all you have to do is add the block slug to the `REGISTERED_BLOCKS` array in `inc/app/Controllers/BlockController.php`. This array assumes your blocks source files are located in the `src/blocks` folder and built to `build/blocks` folder.
